    "updated_at": "2020-10-06T07:02:15Z",
    "body": "Yeah. I don't think we've been keeping careful track of the minimum rustc version needed, but that one seems to be from late last year. Is that the compiler provided by Ubuntu 20.04? You should be able to get a newer version from [rustup.rs](https://rustup.rs/).\r\n\r\nOn my devbox (which is admittedly not Ubuntu), 1.40 and 1.41 fail to build with the error you reported, 1.42 fails with another error, and 1.43 works fine. So if you can install rustc 1.43 or newer, you should be able to build `starship`. The default toolchain that ships with rustup right now is 1.46, so if you visit there, install rustup, and then do `rustup install stable`, you should be good to go.\r\n\r\n",
